        "url": "https://lethain.com/revised-rules-of-engineering-leadership/",
        "description": "\"This post documents the new rules I’ve revised my approach to engineering leadership around, and then talks through the specific projects I’ve worked on over the past year that caused me to believe in these rules.\"\n\nAI changes the pace of engineering, but not the bottlenecks that actually matter\n\nWill Larson’s revised rules? Yes, migrations are cheaper, first-pass code is abundant, and individual engineers can now drive changes that once required teams. The limiting factors still look familiar: harness quality, team domain context, organizational alignment, and the ability to make durable decisions quickly. The essay’s claim is that AI does not erase management or architecture, AI raises the cost of getting them wrong, because judgment now propagates through systems much faster than before.",
